-- title:
--   Sidorenko's inequality for sides of size at most $1$
-- statement:
--   **The rung $r=1$ of the scaled Sidorenko conjecture.** For every finite graph $H$ admitting a bipartition with at most one vertex on each side, and every finite graph $G$ with at least one vertex,
--
--   $$t(H,G)\ \ge\ t(K_2,G)^{\,e(H)}.$$
--
--   Such an $H$ has at most two vertices and at most one edge.
-- source:
--   Elementary; covered by A. F. Sidorenko, Inequalities for functionals generated by bipartite graphs, Discrete Math. Appl. 2 (1992), https://doi.org/10.1515/dma.1992.2.5.489 (bipartite graphs with at most four vertices on one side)

